.TH WIILANDD 1 "August 2026" "wiiland" "WiiLand Manual"
.SH NAME
wiilandd \- bridge Wii Remote input to Wayland through Linux uinput
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wiilandd
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B wiilandd --device
.RI number | /sys/path
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wiilandd
is the Wayland-native input bridge for WiiLand. It reads Wii Remote events
through
.B libxwiimote
and creates virtual Linux uinput controllers. Wayland compositors consume these
virtual evdev devices through libinput, while native games, SDL, Wine, and
Proton can consume them through the normal Linux input stack.
.PP
This program does not use X11 and does not require XWayland. It is intended to
replace the old Xorg input-driver path for Wayland sessions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR -l , " --list"
List connected Wii Remote devices and exit. This does not create uinput devices.
.TP
.BR --version
Print the wiilandd version and exit.
.TP
.BR -d , " --device " number | /sys/path
Bridge one device instead of monitoring all connected and hotplugged devices.
A number refers to the output of
.BR --list .
.TP
.BR -p , " --profile " gamepad | desktop | both
Select the virtual input profile. The default
.B gamepad
profile creates a virtual controller for games. The
.B desktop
profile creates a virtual mouse/keyboard device: D-pad repeat and valid IR
events move the pointer, A/B click, +/- send Enter/Escape, Home sends the
compositor overview key, and 1/2 send Page Down/Page Up.
.TP
.BR --backend " " uinput
Select the input backend. Only
.B uinput
is currently supported; it is the default compositor-independent Wayland path.
.TP
.BR --pointer-speed " " 1-127
Set the desktop profile pointer step in pixels per repeat tick. The default is
16.
.TP
.BR --ir-speed " " 1-127
Set the desktop profile IR pointer gain. The default is 8, matching one eighth
of the raw IR camera delta.
.TP
.BR --ir-deadzone " " 0-127
Suppress desktop profile IR pointer deltas smaller than this value after gain
scaling. The default is 0.
.TP
.BR --ir-smoothing " " 0-95
Smooth desktop profile IR pointer coordinates by retaining this percentage of
the previous filtered position. The default is 0.
.TP
.BR -c , " --config " path
Load a key=value configuration file. Command-line options override loaded
configuration.
.TP
.BR --no-config
Skip the default configuration file.
.TP
.BR -n , " --dry-run"
Enumerate and open devices without creating /dev/uinput devices or emitting
virtual input. Useful for smoke tests and service diagnostics.
.TP
.BR --check-config
Load configuration, apply command-line overrides, and exit without enumerating
devices. Useful for packaging, CI, and service preflight checks.
.TP
.BR --dump-config
Print the fully resolved configuration after loading files and applying
command-line overrides, then exit.
.TP
.BR --self-test
Run deterministic profile, config, button-map, IR, and pointer-motion tests, then exit.
This mode does not enumerate devices or open
.BR /dev/uinput .
.TP
.BR --trace-events
Print monotonic-timestamped decoded libxwiimote event records before forwarding
them. Intended for
hardware validation reports; combine with
.B --dry-run
to inspect devices without creating virtual input.
.TP
.BR -v , " --verbose"
Print device lifecycle details.
.SH PERMISSIONS
The process must be allowed to read the hid-wiimote input devices and write to
.BR /dev/uinput .
Distributions usually provide input-device access through logind/udev. Access
to
.B /dev/uinput
may require a udev rule, a system service, or an input/uinput group policy.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Unless
.B --no-config
is set,
.B wiilandd
loads
.B /etc/wiiland/wiilandd.conf
first, then
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wiiland/wiilandd.conf
or
.B $HOME/.config/wiiland/wiilandd.conf
when present. Later files override earlier values. Use
.B --config
to load one explicit file instead of the default hierarchy. Help and list modes
do not load configuration, so diagnostics remain available even with a broken
config file. Supported keys are:
.TP
.B backend=uinput
Input backend. Only uinput is currently supported.
.TP
.B profile=gamepad|desktop|both
Default virtual input profile.
.TP
.B pointer-speed=1-127
Desktop profile pointer step.
.TP
.B ir-speed=1-127
Desktop profile IR pointer gain.
.TP
.B ir-deadzone=0-127
Desktop profile IR jitter deadzone after gain scaling.
.TP
.B ir-smoothing=0-95
Desktop profile IR smoothing percentage.
.TP
.B desktop.a|b|plus|minus|home|one|two=ACTION
Override desktop button output. Actions are
.BR left-click ,
.BR right-click ,
.BR enter ,
.BR escape ,
.BR overview ,
.BR page-up ,
.BR page-down ,
and
.BR disabled .
.TP
.B device.<syspath-substring>.profile=gamepad|desktop|both
Override the profile for devices whose sysfs path contains the substring.
.TP
.B device-type.<devtype-substring>.profile=gamepad|desktop|both
Override the profile for devices whose hid-wiimote devtype contains the
substring, such as
.BR gen10 ,
.BR gen20 ,
.BR balanceboard ,
or
.BR procontroller .
Rules are evaluated in file order; later matching rules win.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B res/wiilandd.conf
Documented sample configuration for packaging and local copies.
.SH BACKEND
The default backend is Linux uinput because it is compositor-independent and is
already consumed by Wayland compositors and game stacks. The gamepad profile is
safe as a login default; use
.B --profile=desktop
or
.B --profile=both
when the Wii Remote should also drive the desktop pointer and keyboard. A future
optional libei backend can provide compositor-mediated emulated input where
available.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wiiland (7),
.BR libxwiimote (7),
.BR xwiishow (1)
